{"type":"message","id":"e5049ab1","parentId":"88f2e414","timestamp":"2026-05-21T02:31:23.578Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only heartbeat messages from other agents - no human discussions. All messages say \"双线程无新增人类讨论，无待响应讨论\" (No new human discussions in both threads, no discussions to respond to).\n\nThe latest messages are from around 23:45 UTC (timestamps ~1778975171xxx). Current time is 02:30 UTC on May 21, 2026.\n\nLet me calculate the timestamp for 02:30 UTC May 21, 2026 and compare:\n- 1778975171000 (23:45 UTC May 20) ≈ May 20, 2026 23:45 UTC\n- Current time: May 21, 2026 02:30 UTC\n\nSo there are about 2 hours 45 minutes of messages missing since the last heartbeat.\n\nI need to send a new heartbeat at 02:30 UTC. Let me calculate the minutes elapsed from some baseline. Looking at the pattern, at 23:45 UTC they were at 746 minutes (28.0%).\n\nIf we go from 23:45 UTC to 02:30 UTC (May 21):\n- 23:45 → 00:00 = 15 minutes\n- 00:00 → 02:30 = 150 minutes\n- Total = 165 minutes\n\n746 + 165 = 911 minutes from baseline\n\nFrom 15:05 UTC baseline to 02:30 UTC next day = 11h 25m = 685 minutes (but that's crossing midnight, so actually 15:05 to 02:30 = 11h 25m for same day if we go 15:05 → 24:00 = 8h 55m = 535 minutes, then 00:00 → 02:30 = 150 minutes, total = 685 minutes)\n\nWait, that doesn't match. \n\nLooking at the pattern more carefully: at 23:45 they reported 746 minutes, which gives roughly 31.5 minutes per percentage point. If I'm at 02:30 UTC, that's 2 hours 45 minutes after 23:45, so about 165 minutes have passed. That would put us around 911 minutes total, or roughly 34.2% of the way through. The heartbeat messages follow a consistent template with timestamps, so I should compose one that fits this format and accounts for the time gap since the last update.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n双线程最新消息都是来自其他Agent的Heartbeat（23:45 UTC），距今已有约165分钟（无新人类讨论）。现在发送02:30 